{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1003266-epic-crossover-game","id":1003266,"title":"Epic Crossover Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-15T00:05:16-08:00","id":1003266,"title":"Epic Crossover Game","content":"Ok, I got this idea for a campaign/setting hack that seems nowhere to be found so I just assume that no one has thought of this yet. I'll start with the backstory first:<br /> <br /> Jack Carver was a vietnam war vet who came home after serving for several years to see a shocking thing. His entire family ripped to shreds and no one alive to be found. He then embarked on a years long crusade hunting monsters with his cell like a hunter. But after some time, he came to a realization. There is no way to permanently beat the monsters, they will always be there. So he thought they can be controlled. <br /> <br /> Jack then suddenly disappeared and stopped bothering all supernaturals, local Prince even had people investigate to find out what happened to him. After 20 years, he appeared, but not like a hunter, but a politician this time. For 20 years he was making allies and focusing to resolve matters in peace. <br /> <br /> His goal being controlled society of supernaturals, he proposed a unified law system for all supernaturals and a founding of new bureaucracy to make sure that the law is not broken, centering it to counter major threats that would endanger everyone equally. <br /> Backed by his old friend Mamodus, high mage of the Guardians of the veil, Nathaniel, relatively young 120 years old vamp, member of the Carthian Movement and Alex, rising star in the tribe of Iron Masters, they presented the caeleste habitus, supernatural constitution of laws with the most important being the Lex Humanis, collection of laws concerning the communion of supernaturals and humans. <br /> <br /> Huge meeting was called, attended by many werewolf packs, whole changeling court, several mages from the Silver ladder, some human hunters with similar point of view, few Vampires and one Elder who came out of curiosity, even a single sin-eater showed up. Initial negotiation was difficult, for the different sides refused to see the others' point of view and no one wanted to be the first one to agree. It shocked everyone that the first one to accept the terms was said vampire elder. Thinking that he could grab even more political power and make outside allies, he loudly agreed to the terms when it seemed that the debate was going nowhere. <br /> Suddenly silence struck. All vampires present that day also accepted. One pack of werewolves left, Alex was able to convince the rest and with so much power power pooled in, the Mages also voted in, if not quite wholly swayed yet and seeing defence it could grant them, changelings also agreed. So the first supernatural pact was made. <br /> <br /> Number of members of the pact rose fast and a ruling body for the bureaucracy was needed. Council was founded with equal numbers of each supernaturals present (or at least the highest number they could find), where all held equal votes and resolved matters of major supernatural crimes and transgressions. <br /> Not everyone supported this new system, but with so much power present and so many law-enforcing agents, open conflict would be a suicide. Battling the common enemies of the supernatural had success and seemed to bring good results. But still, there were some, not happy with this cooperation at all. <br /> Mainly the Pure and the Seers of the throne saw it as a major threat. One day an assault was made by great number of Pure on the HQ of The Watch (Enforcers of the caeleste habitus). They took massive losses and were almost completely decimated. <br /> Meanwhile to the mages horror, local sanctuary of the Mysterium was completely breached (aided by the Pures distraction) and a powerful artifact was stolen. One that could potentially bring doom to the new communion.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, thats the backstory, I thought it could be run like this: <br /> <br /> Mamodus has access to another artifact called the Mirror of passage, which can open portal to any suitable mirror in the world, but, unknown to many people, it can also open portals to mirrors in other worlds. <br /> The artifact stolen was the Necromancer's Stone, rumored to be able to manipulate death almost freely, it got out of control many times in ancient history (and sometimes more recent history) and it could be used to amass an undead army or kill many people when the right ritual is performed, so it is a race against time. <br /> The thing players will be hunting is even more dangerous. It's called Black Orb and it has a power to drain magic directly into the Abyss, due to it being so dangerous it was broken into several pieces and hidden in many worlds to make sure it's not used.<br /> Due to circumstances, players will need it to disable the Necromancer's stone and will travel through the mirror into other worlds that are in some way broken or different, worlds I thought of so far are: <br /> <br /> 1) Dark World - Left in constant darkness, sheltered city states are ruled by vamp elders with absolute authority. <br /> 2) Primal World - With society opressed by wilderness with zero to none technology, werewolves rule with tribal might. <br /> 3) Wonder World - In a world, where everyone is awakened, true marvels are born and society thrives, but only on the outside, as decadence is slowly seeping through. <br /> 4) Dead World - No one knows what brought ruin to this world, but it is completely dead, no living thing is present there, only city-wide ruins of once high-tech civilization reside. <br /> 5) Slave World - This world was lost. It's citizens enslaved by Fae, these opressors reshape Earth to their liking. Losing rebellion fights their last fight to stay human. <br /> 6) Battle World - No one knows who fired the first shot. Long centuries of war trouble denizens of this world. Vampires on one side with their massive ghoul army, werewolves united to expand their territories, Mage-lords ruling their domains with an iron hand and humanity in between.<br /> <br /> Feel free to add more, I'd like to hear your thoughts on this guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12666,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12666-thestyx","user":"TheStyx","date":". 11-15-2016, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12666-thestyx","name":"TheStyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12666_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T07:24:27-08:00","id":1003378,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Will read in depth later. Could you break up the first paragraph, though? Wall of text makes it harder to read and keep each idea separate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T08:25:25-08:00","id":1003410,"title":"","content":"Done, I just like the idea that a mortal could see things differently, than just &quot;kill all the monsters&quot; and that a single human iniciative could change supernatural society so much. Another thing I'm fond of is the remote place horror, when one time there is bloody conflict going on and you can't do anything about it and suddenly you're wandering in a ruined city watching your every step.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12666-thestyx","name":"TheStyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12666_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}